#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124374 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124565 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f23c5c7-d281-54da-b625-412925c80667" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Differential of a Multivariable Function"}] :question/id #uuid "8ebce398-b228-51b0-8506-e0c6124478a5" :question/math-academy-id "e-6852" :question/problem "Find the differential for $f(x,y) = x^2 \\sin y.$" :question/worked-solution "We compute the differential using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =(2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)\\,\\text{d}x+({x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\text{d}x+{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124375 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124566 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "153739f2-df62-5baf-8438-225edfc33ecb" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Differential in a Geometrical Context"}] :question/id #uuid "bb3ab0dc-7e26-58f5-a0c2-564c01c77f2e" :question/math-academy-id "e-6854" :question/problem "Given a cone, find the differential $\\textrm d V$ for the volume $V$ of the cone if the radius is $r=6$ and the height is $h = 3.$" :question/worked-solution "The volume of the cone is $V = \\dfrac{1}{3} \\pi r^2h.$ Let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}V(r,h) & =(\\frac{∂V}{∂r})\\,\\text{d}r+(\\frac{∂V}{∂h})\\,\\text{d}h \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\pi rh\\,\\text{d}r+\\frac{1}{3}\\pi {r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}h.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $r=6$ and $h=3,$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}V(6,3) & =\\frac{2}{3}\\pi \\cdot 6\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}r+\\frac{1}{3}\\pi \\cdot {6}^{2}\\,\\text{d}h \\\\  & =12\\pi \\,\\text{d}r+12\\pi \\,\\text{d}h.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124376 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124567 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab023be2-0156-5de6-8843-5b720775d649" :knowledge-point/title "Using Differentials to Approximate the Change in a Multivariable Function"}] :question/id #uuid "0c4816ed-fba0-5dc7-94ba-646b875d653d" :question/math-academy-id "e-6875" :question/problem "If $f (x, y) = xe^y ,$ use the differential $\\textrm d f$ to estimate the change $\\Delta f$ in the value of $f(x, y)$ from $(5,0)$ to $(2,1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}x+x{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $(5,0),$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(5,0) & ={e}^{0}\\,\\text{d}x+5{e}^{0}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =1\\,\\text{d}x+5\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(5 + \\Delta x, 0 + \\Delta y),$ then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\n\\Delta f \\approx 1 \\, \\Delta x + 5 \\, \\Delta y.\n$$\n\nMoving from $(5,0)$ to $(2,1),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δx & =2-5=-3, \\\\ Δy & =1-0=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf & ≈1\\,Δx+5\\,Δy \\\\  & ≈1\\cdot (-3)+5\\cdot (1) \\\\  & ≈2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $f(x,y)$ increases by approximately $2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124377 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124568 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "acafc931-a294-5ca7-8e39-cf8be29f08a9" :knowledge-point/title "Using Differentials to Approximate the Value of a Function"}] :question/id #uuid "febc72d4-b1b8-52c9-a805-013b30695077" :question/math-academy-id "e-6876" :question/problem "Estimate $\\sin (3) + \\cos (0.2)$ using a differential of the function $f(x,y) = \\sin x + \\cos y$ at the point $\\left( \\pi, 0 \\right).$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $\\left( \\pi, 0 \\right),$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi \\,\\text{d}x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡0\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =-1\\,\\text{d}x+0\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(\\pi + \\Delta x, 0 + \\Delta y),$ then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\n\\Delta f \\approx  -1  \\,  \\Delta x + 0  \\,  \\Delta y\n$$\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n\\sin (3) + \\cos (0.2)= f(3,0.2),\n$$\n\nso we want to move to the point $(3,0.2).$\n\nMoving from $(\\pi, 0)$ to $(3,0.2),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δx & =3-\\pi ≈-0.141, \\\\ Δy & =0.2-0=0.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf & ≈-1(-0.141)+0(0.2) \\\\  & ≈0.141.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that the value of $f$ increases by about $0.141.$ Consequently, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(3,0.2) & ≈f(\\pi ,0)+0.141 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0.2) & ≈\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)+0.141 \\\\  & ≈0+1+0.141 \\\\  & ≈1.141.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284578 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124567 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab023be2-0156-5de6-8843-5b720775d649" :knowledge-point/title "Using Differentials to Approximate the Change in a Multivariable Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6165f20f-a911-5f52-b154-c9b7146be783" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282518} {:answer/id #uuid "7c25c165-90a1-52b3-950c-0524d0a78d44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282758} {:answer/id #uuid "c9fc9fa5-06d8-5791-9f28-2f5da3679ea4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283452} {:answer/id #uuid "d1675874-99c7-53bb-a75e-8153ff7cfa34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283517} {:answer/id #uuid "ec5c20cb-3aaf-53d0-987f-6298d27bfd52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283756}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c9fc9fa5-06d8-5791-9f28-2f5da3679ea4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283452} :answer-field/id #uuid "8707a5fd-f08d-52ad-bc81-12c73efa5a28" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284168}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7ec3ee1a-9141-5963-a032-74283a58c8bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-167168" :question/problem "If $f(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xyz),$ use the differential $\\text{d}f$ to estimate the change $Δf$ in the value of $f(x,y,z)$ from $(1,1,1)$ to $(2,3,4).$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y,z) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y+(\\frac{∂f}{∂z})\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y+\\frac{1}{z}\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $(1,1,1),$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(1,1,1) & =1\\,\\text{d}x+1\\,\\text{d}y+1\\,\\text{d}z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(1+Δx,1+Δy,1+Δz),$ then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\nΔf≈Δx+Δy+Δz.\n$$\n\nMoving from $(1,1,1)$ to $(2,3,4),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δx & =2-1=1, \\\\ Δy & =3-1=2 \\\\ Δz & =4-1=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf & ≈Δx+Δy+Δz \\\\  & ≈1+2+3 \\\\  & ≈6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $f(x,y,z)$ increases by approximately $6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372349 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124566 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "153739f2-df62-5baf-8438-225edfc33ecb" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Differential in a Geometrical Context"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b0b745db-632d-5d42-b0cb-5988bdfee9f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15\\,\\text{d}a+10\\text{d}b+12\\,\\text{d}h" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372351} {:answer/id #uuid "883260a4-04ea-5104-a33b-20e8f9ddd2f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\,\\text{d}a+15\\text{d}b+10\\,\\text{d}h" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372352} {:answer/id #uuid "643fcc04-a886-51b8-b744-bc0e4ca00b64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9\\,\\text{d}a+8\\text{d}b+10\\,\\text{d}h" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372353} {:answer/id #uuid "71ae431e-e7e1-5107-b656-de08bcff04a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30\\,\\text{d}a+20\\text{d}b+24\\,\\text{d}h" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372354} {:answer/id #uuid "84c9935a-e18a-5e11-96e5-9d9b09b670a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,\\text{d}a+4\\text{d}b+12\\,\\text{d}h" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372355}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0b745db-632d-5d42-b0cb-5988bdfee9f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15\\,\\text{d}a+10\\text{d}b+12\\,\\text{d}h" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372351} :answer-field/id #uuid "22fd4b2f-5a66-564b-904f-0e3de82edda3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372350}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8ad2cde7-ba79-5b5e-a983-25dd72f62433" :question/math-academy-id "q-168149" :question/problem "Given a right triangular prism, find the differential $\\text{d}V$ for the volume $V$ if the height is $h=5$ and the base is a right triangle with legs $a=4$ and $b=6.$" :question/worked-solution "The volume of a given right triangular prism is $V=\\frac{abh}{2}.$ Let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}V(a,b,c) & =(\\frac{∂V}{∂a})\\,\\text{d}a+(\\frac{∂V}{∂b})\\,\\text{d}b+(\\frac{∂V}{∂h})\\,\\text{d}h \\\\  & =\\frac{bh}{2}\\,\\text{d}a+\\frac{ah}{2}\\,\\text{d}b+\\frac{ab}{2}\\,\\text{d}h\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $a=4,$ $b=6,$ and $h=5,$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}V(4,6,5) & =\\frac{6\\cdot 5}{2}\\,\\text{d}a+\\frac{4\\cdot 5}{2}\\,\\text{d}b+\\frac{4\\cdot 6}{2}\\,\\text{d}h \\\\  & =15\\,\\text{d}a+10\\text{d}b+12\\,\\text{d}h.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284605 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124566 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "153739f2-df62-5baf-8438-225edfc33ecb" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Differential in a Geometrical Context"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30ff9de6-82b9-57fd-8352-549a13be4d7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36\\,\\text{d}a+9\\,\\text{d}b+64\\,\\text{d}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282128} {:answer/id #uuid "4ae0312d-ecd7-57dc-9d88-15ff8ec29a6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18\\,\\text{d}a+24\\,\\text{d}b+48\\,\\text{d}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282330} {:answer/id #uuid "55b45edc-b405-5927-afc4-f43852758102" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24\\,\\text{d}a+48\\,\\text{d}b+18\\,\\text{d}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282415} {:answer/id #uuid "8abb4554-2c3b-5729-8dbb-6cd315e8c4a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,\\text{d}a+3\\,\\text{d}b+9\\,\\text{d}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282885} {:answer/id #uuid "e3a31cef-0e81-5be3-8ef5-5772fcc10f4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\,\\text{d}a+24\\,\\text{d}b+9\\,\\text{d}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283675}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "55b45edc-b405-5927-afc4-f43852758102" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24\\,\\text{d}a+48\\,\\text{d}b+18\\,\\text{d}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282415} :answer-field/id #uuid "8563a43e-521b-5142-9d50-25857d86ed4c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284160}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "56bdc966-10cb-53e1-a679-ccd338b6c565" :question/math-academy-id "q-168150" :question/problem "Given a rectangular solid, find the differential $\\text{d}V$ for the volume $V$ of the rectangular solid if the lengths of the sides are $a=6,$ $b=3,$ and $c=8.$" :question/worked-solution "The volume of the rectangular solid is $V=abc.$ Let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}V(a,b,c) & =(\\frac{∂V}{∂a})\\,\\text{d}a+(\\frac{∂V}{∂b})\\,\\text{d}b+(\\frac{∂V}{∂c})\\,\\text{d}c \\\\  & =bc\\,\\text{d}a+ac\\,\\text{d}b+ab\\,\\text{d}c\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $a=6,$ $b=3,$ and $c=8,$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}V(6,3,8) & =3\\cdot 8\\,\\text{d}a+6\\cdot 8\\,\\text{d}b+6\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}c \\\\  & =24\\,\\text{d}a+48\\,\\text{d}b+18\\,\\text{d}c.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125051 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124568 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "acafc931-a294-5ca7-8e39-cf8be29f08a9" :knowledge-point/title "Using Differentials to Approximate the Value of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b48ae87-4176-58e0-812f-d85f6773ef32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11.215" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321605} {:answer/id #uuid "3d19300c-6ea3-57b7-95c7-ec16fb63521e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15.873" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321622} {:answer/id #uuid "499e8720-d131-55b2-ba8b-eed19cb2b0cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10.235" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321725} {:answer/id #uuid "90606f37-bff4-5fe0-962f-40b81e027f91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18.556" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322292} {:answer/id #uuid "b89c9f1a-e6f4-5b65-b8c8-c7617859f22f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14.417" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322581}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b89c9f1a-e6f4-5b65-b8c8-c7617859f22f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14.417" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322581} :answer-field/id #uuid "323fec80-bc80-56a8-ad29-27e2aee73e54" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323271}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c4f3d8c4-d372-512f-a12b-325fd0cb0744" :question/math-academy-id "q-37281" :question/problem "Estimate $\\sqrt[3]{10}+\\sqrt{150}$ using a differential $\\text{d}f$ of the function $f(x,y)=\\sqrt[3]{x}+\\sqrt{y}$ at the point $(8,144).$ Round your answer to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3{x}^{2/3}}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{y}}\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $(8,144),$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{3\\cdot {8}^{2/3}}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{144}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{24}\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(8+Δx,144+Δy),$ then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\nΔf≈\\frac{1}{12}\\,Δx+\\frac{1}{24}\\,Δy\n$$\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n\\sqrt[3]{10}+\\sqrt{150}=f(10,150),\n$$\n\nso we want to move to the point $(10,150).$\n\nMoving from $(8,144)$ to $(10,150),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δx & =10-8=2, \\\\ Δy & =150-144=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf & ≈\\frac{1}{12}(2)+\\frac{1}{24}(6) \\\\  & ≈\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & ≈\\frac{5}{12} \\\\  & ≈0.417.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that the value of $f$ increases by about $0.417.$ Consequently, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(10,150) & ≈f(8,144)+0.417 \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{10}+\\sqrt{150} & ≈\\sqrt[3]{8}+\\sqrt{144}+0.417 \\\\  & ≈2+12+0.417 \\\\  & ≈14.417.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125052 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124565 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f23c5c7-d281-54da-b625-412925c80667" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Differential of a Multivariable Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "819d161a-21cf-535e-bd37-4754ea1a38e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-y\\sin ydx - (2z^{2} - x\\sin x)dy - 4yzdz" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122913} {:answer/id #uuid "c9f41994-af80-51f0-a777-c868bf2016f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-y\\sin (xy)dx - (2z^{2} + x\\sin (xy))dy - 4yzdz" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122914} {:answer/id #uuid "d7ff6632-8a2c-51e3-a5d2-71c9bb45bfda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2z^{2} + (x - y)\\sin (xy) - 4yz" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122915} {:ans